{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1248815-which-umbra-book-should-i-read","id":1248815,"title":"Which Umbra Book Should I Read?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-22T21:33:33-07:00","id":1248815,"title":"Which Umbra Book Should I Read?","content":"So my group is gearing up to play a mixed game of Classic World of Darkness, 3/5 of the group being Werewolf the Apocalypse characters, after having read about the Umbra from the Revised Source book for Werewolf the Apocalypse I want to do a lot of Umbra stuff, so I wanna read more about it.<br /> <br /> The obvious choice is Umbra (Revised) but I've heard good things about W20 Umbra: The Velvet Shadow and we are using some W20 influence too, we mainly settled on Revised because W20 hasn't fleshed out as much yet. There are even more Umbra books too, so I wanna know what you guys recommend as the best read for Umbra lore and mechanics and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24503-wulfswift","name":"Wulfswift","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-23T03:22:46-07:00","id":1248830,"title":"","content":"W20 Umbra, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T00:12:34-07:00","id":1249070,"title":"","content":"Umbra revised was a very important book for me, and one of my very favorite RPG books in general, I\u2019m biased because I love it so much and it\u2019s still viable. But W20 Umbra is also good and gives some alternatives. Some things are different, like the Serpent of Pangea is now a great winged dragon and I\u2019m not keen on that. But both works. Also Rage Across the Heavena are also fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T07:59:01-07:00","id":1249137,"title":"","content":"W20 Umbra is really damn good, but the Revised Edition one and Rage Across the Heavens are also worth your time","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/nbylxup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n77xu8p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"lin